<% content_for :title, "Styles — shadcnrb" %>

<div class="space-y-8">
  <div class="space-y-2">
    <%= sui.h1 "Styles" %>
    <%= sui.lead do %>
      A <strong>style</strong> swaps the Tailwind class strings each component
      returns. Themes change colors via CSS tokens; styles change structure —
      border thickness, corner radius, shadow offset, typography.
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%= sui.separator %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Declaring a style" %>
    <%= sui.p do %>
      Put override classes under <%= sui.code "Shadcnrb::Styles::<Name>" %> —
      one per component, named after the component module. Each overrides
      whichever methods on the parent <%= sui.code "Style" %> class it wants
      to change.
    <% end %>
    <% code = <<~RUBY
      # app/components/shadcnrb/styles/brutalist.rb
      module Shadcnrb::Styles::Brutalist
        class Button < Shadcnrb::Button::Style
          def base
            "inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-none border-2 border-black " \\
              "font-bold uppercase tracking-wide shadow-[4px_4px_0_0_#000]"
          end
        end
      end
    RUBY
    %>
    <%= sui.codeblock code, syntax: :ruby %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Applying a style" %>
    <% code = <<~RUBY
      Shadcnrb::Style.apply(:brutalist)   # flip the look
      Shadcnrb::Style.reset               # back to defaults
    RUBY
    %>
    <%= sui.codeblock code, syntax: :ruby %>
    <%= sui.p do %>
      <%= sui.code "apply" %> resets first, then finds each override class by
      name and assigns a new instance to the matching component. No
      <%= sui.code "apply!" %> boilerplate, no COMPONENTS hash — just the
      class definitions.
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Per-request application" %>
    <%= sui.p do %>
      Styles are server-side global state. Apply the active one in a
      <%= sui.code "before_action" %> so each request renders with the right
      classes:
    <% end %>
    <% code = <<~RUBY
      class ApplicationController < ActionController::Base
        before_action :apply_shadcnrb_style

        private

        def apply_shadcnrb_style
          Shadcnrb::Style.apply(cookies[:shadcnrb_style])
        end
      end
    RUBY
    %>
    <%= sui.codeblock code, syntax: :ruby %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Reference implementation" %>
    <%= sui.p do %>
      This example app ships
      <%= sui.code "Shadcnrb::Styles::Neobrutalism" %> covering every visual
      component. Pick <strong>Neobrutalism</strong> in the style switcher at
      the top of the page to see it live, or read the full source at
      <%= sui.link_to "app/components/shadcnrb/styles/neobrutalism.rb",
                      "https://github.com/AccountAim/shadcn-rb-example/blob/main/app/components/shadcnrb/styles/neobrutalism.rb",
                      variant: :underline, target: "_blank" %>.
    <% end %>
    <%= sui.p do %>
      Pair with a user-facing picker — see
      <%= sui.link_to "StyleSwitcherHelper",
                      "https://github.com/AccountAim/shadcn-rb-example/blob/main/app/helpers/style_switcher_helper.rb",
                      variant: :underline, target: "_blank" %>
      and its
      <%= sui.link_to "Stimulus controller",
                      "https://github.com/AccountAim/shadcn-rb-example/blob/main/app/javascript/controllers/style_switcher_controller.js",
                      variant: :underline, target: "_blank" %>
      in this repo. The pick is a cookie written client-side plus a reload —
      no POST, so it keeps working on pages served without a session.
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
